d 'PROJECTBUILDER': module to scaffold a data-analysis project folder with a numbered do-file pipeline
d
d  projectbuilder builds a project folder in one command: a
d raw-data folder, an analytic-data folder, an output folder, a
d documentation folder, and a numbered do-file pipeline
d (000_control through 600_analysis). A control file holds every
d path in one place and can run the whole pipeline. If you already
d have the data, point data() at local files or url() at a source
d address and projectbuilder copies it in and writes a
d documentation page; with the optional convertanything and
d combineall installed it also converts each raw file and appends
d them into one analytic file. If the data comes later, scaffold
d now and rerun with rebuild on every refresh; rebuild never
d overwrites a do-file you have edited unless you add replace. The
d tool is self-contained (every file is written by the program, no
d template folder), uses only Stata's cross-platform file commands,
d and never overwrites an existing project. Optional companions add
d power when installed but are never required: convertanything and
d combineall (author's GitHub), descsave (SSC), srctag/srcfind
d (author's GitHub), and webdoc2 (author's GitHub). The command
d leaves the dataset in memory untouched. A test battery ships with
d the package as an ancillary file; retrieve it with -net get
d projectbuilder- and run it with -do test_projectbuilder.do-. 
d
d KW: reproducible research; project management; workflow; do-files
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
d Author: Elizabeth Teas, Far Harbor, LLC
d Support: email elizabeth@@farharbor.com
d
f projectbuilder.ado
f projectbuilder.sthlp
f ../t/test_projectbuilder.do
